    "created_at": "2018-08-02T14:39:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-02T14:39:52Z",
    "body": "The browser or its extensions can somehow disable or block any scripts, including inline scripts. So I'd like to see a pure CSS mechanism to give users information about load failure without script code.\r\n\r\nAlso, I think automatically adding a `load-failure` attribute when an element with `report-load-failure` is a semantical content for a document. Currently, there's no way for the document itself to reflect the semantical fact that something has failed to load.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
