    "updated_at": "2018-08-02T14:46:38Z",
    "body": "@Zhang-Junzhi thanks for clarifying, wouldn't a meta property without requiring a CSS attribute make more sense? \r\n\r\n```css\r\nimg:load-failure {\r\n  /* do something with the fact the image or script did not load */ \r\n}\r\n\r\nhtml:has(script:load-failure) body::before {\r\n  content: \"Failed to load some necessary....\";\r\n}\r\n\r\n```",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
